\end{aligned}=\frac{10\left(\sec ^{10} \theta+\cos ^{10} \theta\right)}{\sec \theta+\cos \theta}\begin{aligned} \therefore \quad\left(\frac{\mathrm{d} y}{\mathrm{~d} x}\right)^2 & =\frac{10^2\left(\sec ^{10} \theta+\cos ^{10} \theta\right)^2}{(\sec \theta+\cos \theta)^2} \\ & =\frac{100\left[\left(\sec ^{10} \theta-\cos ^{10} \theta\right)^2+4 \sec ^{10} \theta \cos ^{10} \theta\right]}{(\sec \theta-\cos \theta)^2+4 \sec \theta \cos \theta}\end{aligned}\begin{aligned} \therefore \quad & \left(\frac{d y}{d x}\right)^2=\frac{100\left(y^2+4\right)}{x^2+4} \\ & \Rightarrow\left(x^2+4\right)\left(\frac{d y}{d x}\right)^2=100\left(y^2+4\right) \Rightarrow \mathrm{k}=100\end{aligned}$

